ROSE's C/C++ front end: EDG
===========================

ROSE parses C and C++ with the EDG front end and translates EDG's intermediate language
into ROSE's SageIII AST. This directory holds everything ROSE adds around EDG:

  edg_compiler/   git submodule: the EDG C/C++ front end (open source, Apache-2.0 WITH
                  LLVM-exception, github.com/edgcpp/compiler) from the public fork
                  https://github.com/rose-compiler/edg, branch rose/<version>. The branch is
                  the upstream release tag plus ROSE's patches as individual commits; see
                  ROSE-PATCHES.md inside it. Upstream layout: src/*.c (compiled as C++),
                  util/, include_c++/ ...

  edg_build/      ROSE's configuration of EDG for the CMake build: macro-conf/rose/*.cmakedef
                  (EDG's own configuration format) plus CMakeLists.txt, which generates the
                  host-dependent part and the dettarg target description into the build tree.
                  EDG's CMake project (edg_compiler/CMakeLists.txt, added as a subdirectory by
                  CMakeLists.txt here) turns that set into cmake_defines.h and builds the front
                  end as the static library edg_frontend (edg_add_frontend_library, see
                  edg_compiler/cmake/frontend-library.cmake); no source list lives in ROSE.
                  Makefile.am, defines.h.rose and the *.sh helpers are the deprecated autotools
                  build of the same thing (not maintained; the cmakedef set is authoritative).

  edgRose/        the EDG IL -> SageIII translator (ROSE code). Compiled into libnewsage.la /
                  the edg_rose object library, which links edg_frontend; both go into
                  libroseEDG (autotools) or RoseSourceCxxFrontendEdg (CMake).

  MIGRATION.md    how this directory relates to the former private EDG submodule.

  MACOS-STATUS.md state of the macOS / Apple Silicon port (EDG 7.0, Apple clang, libc++):
                  what works, what fails and why, pending issues and next tasks.

Getting the EDG source
----------------------

    git submodule update --init src/frontend/CxxFrontend/EDG/edg_compiler

The submodule is required whenever ROSE is configured with C/C++ support and without the Clang
frontend; configure and CMake stop with that instruction if it is missing. The EDG version ROSE
builds against is read from edg_compiler/src/version.h. (Earlier ROSE releases downloaded a
precompiled EDG library instead; that mechanism no longer exists.)

Upgrading EDG
-------------

See scripts/edg-upgrade.md: the ROSE patch series is rebased onto the new upstream tag in the
fork (git rebase --onto), tagged, and the submodule pointer here is moved to the new tag.
edgRose rarely needs changes for a minor EDG release.

Notes on the interface
----------------------

edgRose builds the SageIII AST by traversing EDG's source sequence lists. It replaced the
earlier EDG_SAGE_Connection (EDG 3.x), which generated code via a copy of EDG's unparser.
The changes ROSE needs inside EDG are small and guarded by macros (ENABLE_CUDA_SUPPORT,
LITERALS_AS_STRINGS_SUPPORT, ROSE_MISC, ...); with those undefined the fork behaves as
upstream EDG.
